course: dictionary
lesson: 9266
title: A word to remember
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A souvenir is something you buy or keep to help you remember a place you visited or an event you went to. «Before a trip you decide how much money to spend on souvenirs and keep it safe.» Here, souvenirs are things you buy on a trip so you can remember it later.
explain: Souvenirs are often small things, like a keyring, a postcard or a badge. Read the words around souvenir to find its meaning: the trip, the visit and the match are the clues. Ask yourself what it is for. It is for remembering.
explain: The phrases «souvenir shop», «as a souvenir» and «a souvenir of» show how the word is used. A souvenir of a day out is something that reminds you of that day. Try your meaning in the sentence to check that it makes sense.
fact: A souvenir is something you buy or keep to remember a place or an event.
fact: People buy souvenirs on holidays, at museums and at sports matches.
fact: Keyrings, postcards and badges are common souvenirs.
fact: A «souvenir shop» is a shop that sells souvenirs.
fact: In French, «un souvenir» means a keepsake, but it also means any memory; «se souvenir» means to remember.
fact: Souvenir came into English from French, so it is a borrowed word.
exercise: «Before a trip you decide how much money to spend on souvenirs.» What is a souvenir? | Money you save for a rainy day | *Something you buy or keep to remember a place you visited | A map that shows the way to a park | A ticket you use to get onto a bus
exercise: Which of these is a souvenir from a museum visit? | *A keyring with the museum's name on it | A packet of crisps bought at school | A bus timetable | A broken umbrella
exercise: Which word in these lessons came into English from French? | Kitchen | Breakfast | *Garage | Table
test: «Sam bought a postcard of the castle as a souvenir.» What does «as a souvenir» show? | To hide under the bed | To use as a map of the town | *To keep and remember the castle visit | To send to a teacher about homework
test: In French, what does «un souvenir» also mean? | A kind of train | *Any memory | A shop that sells keyrings | A keepsake only
exam: Mia wants something to remember her trip to the seaside. Which is a souvenir? | A torn ticket she threw away | A bus timetable from the station | A bag of school books | *A shell-shaped keyring from the seaside shop
